  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3404: Medium priority package update for curl",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-09 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-09 15:26:00"
  },
  "severity": "Medium",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-19931:\n\tA flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given hostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done using empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's previously authenticated connection.\n\nCVE-2026-18924:\n\tA flaw in libcurl's handling of HTTP/2 Server Push streams, when the parent handle is set to share connections with other handles, can lead to use-after-free in the cleanup process.\n",
